    {
      "id": "35568454",
      "title": "More on Interfaces",
      "lectureOrder": 76,
      "videoOrder": 75,
      "sourceHash": "4b1b5588ad5a6edcb5a7b00606217c7d2010764144f5b5769ad211473631adc6",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.06,
          "end": 2.43,
          "en": "-: In fact, before talking about the need for interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.43,
          "end": 4.92,
          "en": "we have one more thing to add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.92,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "So let's say if I have a interface and I'm creating a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 10.68,
          "en": "which implements A, one interface here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.68,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "can a class implement multiple interface?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "Example, let's say if I have interface, which is called X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 21.41,
          "en": "So if I say interface X, so B class implements A and X both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "And the answer is yes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 24.54,
          "en": "If you can see, there's no error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.54,
          "end": 26.61,
          "en": "The only thing is whatever method you define here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "so let's say the method name here is run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 31.65,
          "en": "You can see we got an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 32.61,
          "en": "The only thing you have to do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.61,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "you have to define run as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "So you will say public void run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "So basically we can have one class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "implementing multiple interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 43.29,
          "en": "Now that's not the case with abstract class, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.29,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "Because in abstract class, we can extend only one class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 47.273,
          "en": "In interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 47.273,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "you can have a class implementing multiple interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "So here I can simply print running, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "So what we are doing is we are using multiple methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 60.99,
          "en": "We have three methods coming from two different interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 63.96,
          "en": "This interface says two methods, show and config.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.96,
          "end": 67.41,
          "en": "And this interface is, has only one method, which is run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 70.02,
          "en": "And you can see we got three methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.02,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "There's one more thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "Let's say we have one more interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 75.06,
          "en": "which is called interface Y.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 77.55,
          "en": "Now the thing is when you talk about class and class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.55,
          "end": 79.95,
          "en": "a class can extend another class, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 79.95,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "What about interface? But can we do interface and interface?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "What keyword we have to use here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "See, whenever you have interface to interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "we say extends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "So interface Y extends X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "So inheritance is valid here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "Now in this Y interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 98.94,
          "en": "you'll be having a method called run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 98.94,
          "end": 100.14,
          "en": "So that's the inheritance, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 100.14,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "So you will get this declaration in the interface Y as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 105.27000000000001,
          "en": "Let me show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 105.27000000000001,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "If I remove this X and if I keep Y,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 109.8,
          "en": "even now we have to use run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.8,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "Otherwise, if you remove run from here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "if you come in this part, you can see, it'll give you error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.06,
          "en": "It says \"The type B must",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 117.06,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "implement the inherited abstract method run,\" okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "But we are implementing Y, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 128.16,
          "en": "It's just that Y extends X, so we have to use run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 128.16,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "Now point to remember here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 134.54,
          "en": "whenever you have a class to class, we say they extends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "Whenever you have class to interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 140.24,
          "en": "basically a class is implementing interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.24,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "so we have to say implements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 145.68,
          "en": "And whenever you have interface to interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 145.68,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "we say that extends again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "Okay, so this is the point you have to remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "So again, I will uncomment this part, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "Now there's only one thing you have to remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 158.28,
          "en": "Whenever you create a reference of A interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 158.28,
          "end": 160.32,
          "en": "and object of B, which is a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "I can only call two methods, which is of part A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 166.92000000000002,
          "en": "If I try to call run with A, it will not work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 170.73,
          "en": "because A has no idea what run method is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 170.73,
          "end": 173.67000000000002,
          "en": "If you can see in A, we don't have run.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 174.503,
          "en": "In fact, what I will do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 174.503,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "I will just remove this code for time being, yeah.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "And then if you want to implement run,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "if you want to call run, in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 184.5,
          "en": "we need to create the reference of X,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 184.5,
          "end": 187.95,
          "en": "which is obj1 is equal to new B.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 187.95,
          "end": 190.11,
          "en": "Now, with this obj1, I can call run,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 190.11,
          "end": 193.95,
          "en": "but again, I can't call two other methods, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 193.95,
          "end": 195.81,
          "en": "So that's one thing you have to remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 195.81,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "Okay now, once we are good with this, let's try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 201.363,
          "en": "to understand what's the need of the interface.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
